Z||000017||William Federle||08-25-2001||08:13 PM||||I had the same thing happen to my 1984 duke except that no one touches my car but me. It threw an autozone belt and the first indication was the voltmeter going down and the second was the temperature pegging. The coolant overflowed on mine too.<P> I got it towed home and I changed the oil and brought the coolant level back up. <BR>That was about 2 months ago and it's still running - I drive it to and from work every day (about 100 miles).||||reg||1
Z||000018||Songman||08-25-2001||09:57 PM||||Stimpy, change the fluids and drive it... and pray... the dukes are tough... maybe you are okay.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||14
Z||000019||ray b||08-25-2001||10:25 PM||||do a leak down test like a compression test but use compressed air and see how long it takes for the pressure to leak out where it goes tells what is bad rings values gaskets ect. will not hurt car even if something broke inside. good luck<P>------------------<BR>Question wonder and be wierd||||reg||1
Z||000020||GarethWright||08-25-2001||10:28 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Cheever3000:<BR><B>Dang.  I didn't know Broken Arrow was such a late-night kinda town!  Last time I was up there, they rolled up the streets & sidewalks at 11:00 p.m.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Yea no joke, everything but Wal-Mart closes after 9 (it IS interesting seeing which people are in Wal-Mart at 3 AM) but lucky for me, I'm not a natural born resident of B.A.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR>||||reg||1
